Sprites in this directory are NOT covered by the repository's MIT license.
Neither is ../thumbnail.png (mod/jamaltron/thumbnail.png): it is a render of the
same model, and it sits at the mod root only because Factorio reads the mod-list
thumbnail from nowhere else. Everything below applies to it as to the sprites here.

They are renders of "Animated Hammerhead Shark" by Pig Scales Studio, licensed
from RenderHub (https://www.renderhub.com/pig-scales-studio/animated-hammerhead-shark)
under the RenderHub 3D Content Licensing Agreement, Extended Use License.

3D model copyright Pig Scales Studio via RenderHub.

WHAT YOU MAY DO
  Use, copy, modify and redistribute these images AS PART OF THIS MOD, including
  in forks and derivative mods that remain a larger work of their own. That is
  what the Extended Use License permits: a render may travel inside a Creation.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
  Extract these images and redistribute them as standalone art, as a sprite
  pack, as stock media, or upload them to any content marketplace. They may not
  be used outside a larger work.

WHY THE MIT FILE DOES NOT REACH HERE
  The Extended Use License grants no right to sublicense. MIT would purport to
  grant recipients the right to "sublicense, and/or sell copies" - rights the
  repository owner does not hold and therefore cannot pass on. Applying MIT to
  these files would be a material breach terminating the underlying license, so
  it is carved out deliberately rather than by oversight.

The model source files (.blend/.fbx/.dae and textures) are NOT redistributed and
are not present in this repository.
